Inspired by this process, ActorMind, shown in Figure 2, conceptualizes four agents—Eye, Ear, Mouth, and Brain.
The Eye Agent handles character profile and scene script reading;
the Ear Agent focuses on listening to the speech tones of others;
the Brain Agent is responsible for emotion state reasoning;
and, aided by Retrieval Argument Generation (RAG) (Fan et al., 2024; Zhang et al., 2026b), the Mouth Agent delivers the script with the desired emotion and voice by referencing emotionally similar historical speeches.
